&lt;h3&gt;2.1.1 Data Classification&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;211-data-classification&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#211-data-classification&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Identifying and classifying information and assets is a critical first step in developing an
effective security program. This process involves categorising data and assets based on their sensitivity, criticality, strategic, and monetary value to the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prioritise security measures:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensures systems and data are protected through proactive risk mitigation and safeguards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilitates compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Helps meet regulatory and industry standards efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Streamlines access controls:&lt;/strong&gt; Simplifies management of user permissions and secure access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improves incident response:&lt;/strong&gt; Enables faster detection, containment, and resolution of threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reduces risk of data loss:&lt;/strong&gt; Protects critical information from breaches, leaks, or accidental loss.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div
  data-alert=&#34;example&#34; class=&#34;hextra-alert&#34;
&gt;
  &lt;p class=&#34;hextra-alert-title&#34;&gt;&lt;svg height=16px class=&#34;hextra-alert-icon&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; d=&#34;M9.663 17h4.673M12 3v1m6.364 1.636l-.707.707M21 12h-1M4 12H3m3.343-5.657l-.707-.707m2.828 9.9a5 5 0 117.072 0l-.548.547A3.374 3.374 0 0014 18.469V19a2 2 0 11-4 0v-.531c0-.895-.356-1.754-.988-2.386l-.548-.547z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;hextra-alert-title-text&#34;&gt;Incident Response&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hextra-alert-content&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;An incident response team can securely manage sensitive data and continuously monitor for events, triggering alerts when potential data exposure is detected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Common types of sensitive data:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PII / SPII&lt;/strong&gt; – Personally Identifiable Information / Sensitive Personally Identifiable Information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHI&lt;/strong&gt; – Protected Health Information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PFI&lt;/strong&gt; – Personal Financial Information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Anonymisation&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;anonymisation&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#anonymisation&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;The process of permanently removing or altering personal data so that an individual can no longer be identified, directly or indirectly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div
  data-alert=&#34;example&#34; class=&#34;hextra-alert&#34;
&gt;
  &lt;p class=&#34;hextra-alert-title&#34;&gt;&lt;svg height=16px class=&#34;hextra-alert-icon&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; d=&#34;M9.663 17h4.673M12 3v1m6.364 1.636l-.707.707M21 12h-1M4 12H3m3.343-5.657l-.707-.707m2.828 9.9a5 5 0 117.072 0l-.548.547A3.374 3.374 0 0014 18.469V19a2 2 0 11-4 0v-.531c0-.895-.356-1.754-.988-2.386l-.548-.547z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;hextra-alert-title-text&#34;&gt;Anonymisation&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hextra-alert-content&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Before: &lt;code&gt;Alice Lee, alice@email.com, 91234567&lt;/code&gt;
After: &lt;code&gt;User, Age 28, Singapore&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
👉 No way to trace back to Alice&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Pseudonymisation&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;pseudonymisation&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#pseudonymisation&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;The process of replacing identifiable information with artificial identifiers (pseudonyms), where the original identity can still be recovered using additional data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div
  data-alert=&#34;example&#34; class=&#34;hextra-alert&#34;
&gt;
  &lt;p class=&#34;hextra-alert-title&#34;&gt;&lt;svg height=16px class=&#34;hextra-alert-icon&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; d=&#34;M9.663 17h4.673M12 3v1m6.364 1.636l-.707.707M21 12h-1M4 12H3m3.343-5.657l-.707-.707m2.828 9.9a5 5 0 117.072 0l-.548.547A3.374 3.374 0 0014 18.469V19a2 2 0 11-4 0v-.531c0-.895-.356-1.754-.988-2.386l-.548-.547z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;hextra-alert-title-text&#34;&gt;Pseudonymisation&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hextra-alert-content&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Before: &lt;code&gt;Alice Lee, NRIC S1234567A&lt;/code&gt;
After: &lt;code&gt;User ID: U1029&lt;/code&gt;
Mapping table: &lt;code&gt;U1029 → Alice Lee&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
👉 Identity is hidden but &lt;strong&gt;recoverable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Aspect&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Anonymisation&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Pseudonymisation&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Reversible?&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;❌ No&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;✅ Yes (with key)&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Identifiable?&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;❌ Not at all&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;⚠️ Indirectly&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Security level&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;🔒 Higher&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;🔐 Moderate&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Use case&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Data sharing, analytics&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Internal systems, tracking users&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;GDPR classification&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Not personal data&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Still personal data&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Data Classification&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;data-classification&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#data-classification&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gathering requirements:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify what data exists, its sensitivity, and regulatory or business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Classification scheme:&lt;/strong&gt; Define clear categories (e.g., public, internal, confidential) to organize data by sensitivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data labelling:&lt;/strong&gt; Apply tags or labels to data so its classification is visible and enforceable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User training:&lt;/strong&gt; Educate users on how to handle, classify, and protect data appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintenance:&lt;/strong&gt; Regularly review and update classifications to reflect changes in data and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Data classification in government and public organisations:&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;data-classification-in-government-and-public-organisations&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#data-classification-in-government-and-public-organisations&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Government classification are based on the possible damage ti national security, while non-government classification focus on a broader range of harm including financial, reputation damage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d2/assets/Pasted_image_20260715235647.png&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;  loading=&#34;lazy&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;2.1.2 Asset classification&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;212-asset-classification&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#212-asset-classification&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Asset classification involves categorizing assets based on their importance to the organization and the sensitivity of the data they store, process, or transmit. Important aspects of asset classification to remember:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Classify assets based on their value, criticality, and sensitivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consider the data stored, processed, or transmitted by the assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align asset classification with data classification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use asset classification to prioritize security controls and risk management efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

      </description>
